# Copy this file to `.env` and pick ONE database setup.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option A — SQLite (no server to install; ideal for Windows / a fresh laptop).
# The repo ships a ready-built prisma/customs.db, so you can just run the app.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DB_PROVIDER="sqlite"
DATABASE_URL="file:./customs.db"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option B — Postgres (server-based; enables tsvector full-text search).
# Uncomment these two and comment out the SQLite pair above.
#   - Docker:      DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/customs"
#   - Local socket:DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER@localhost:5432/customs?host=/var/run/postgresql"
#   - Neon (cloud):DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/customs?sslmode=require"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_PROVIDER="postgres"
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/customs"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — the AI officer's briefing (lib/ai/).
#
# This is the ONLY feature that reaches the network. Leave it unset and the app
# behaves exactly as it does today: fully offline, and the briefing button is
# never rendered.
#
# Setting it here overrides anything saved on the /settings page and switches
# the feature on, which is how a dev or server deployment configures it without
# writing a key to disk. Desktop users use /settings instead.
#
# What is sent: the deterministic assessment (HS code, rates, legal references,
# pages) plus passages from the loaded public documents. Never the officer's
# typed sentence, and never a trader name, KRA PIN or entry number.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
